# Phase 4, GA-2-13's recheck (2026-10-14): the income tax's yield memo keys everything the yield reads that can move - the boundary's level and
# wage, the line's own rates in full, the committed pyramid (by reference: CohortDemographics.CommitYear swaps in a new array) and the lever's rate
# in full. The finding is latent (no run showed it), so its proof is the trajectories: the sub-row runs, whose keys carry decimals (X-02S, and
# X-02R on the knob's grid with the lever off its seed), and the finding's area, 2. Expected: every run byte-identical to its twin (X-02S against
# p4_ga211, X-02R against p4_ga212c - s828's own code - area 2 against p4_ga212b) unless a real turn read a stale yield; the simulation bar's
# sentinel answers the same question for the no-policy game.
